==English==
{{wp|velocity (disambiguation)|velocity}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|frm|vélocité}}, from {{der|en|la|vēlōcitās||speed}}, from {{m|la|vēlōx||fast}}, thus a {{dbt|en|veloce|nocap=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/vəˈlɒsəti/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/vəˈlɑsəti/|a=GenAm}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-velocity.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɒsɪti|s=4}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|physics}} A [[vector]] [[quantity]] that denotes the rate of change of [[position]] with respect to time, combining [[speed]] with a directional component.
#: {{ux|en|A car racing in a circle may retain the same speed while continually changing its '''velocity'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2004| title=Atmosphere, Weather and Climate |author=Roger Barry, Richard Chorley, Roger G. Barry | page=118| passage=Usually, however, confluence is associated with an increase in air '''velocity''' and diffluence with a decrease. In the intermediate case, confluence is balanced by an increase in wind '''velocity''' and diffluence by a decrease in '''velocity'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2015|date=|author=Robert A. Fesen; Dan Milisavljevic|title=An HST Survey of the Highest-Velocity Ejecta in Cassiopeia A|journal=arXiv|url=http://arxiv.org/abs/1512.05049|doi=|volume=|issue=|pages=
|passage=Such angular distances imply undecelerated ejecta knot transverse '''velocities''' of 15,600 and 12,700 km/s respectively, assuming an explosion date ~1670 AD and a distance of 3.4 kpc. }}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Tom Whipple|title=Microcannon firing nanobullets: the future of targeted medicine|magazine=w:The Times|url=https://www.thetimes.com/uk/science/article/microcannon-firing-nanobullets-the-future-of-targeted-medicine-h8nhjsbd2nd|date=2016-02-01|passage=When an ultrasonic beam is fired at the microcannons, the emulsion evaporates, expanding rapidly into gas. This creates enough force to push the nanobullets out at '''velocities''' reaching several metres per second.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Ashley Strickland|title=An unusual object is moving so fast it could escape the Milky Way. Scientists aren’t certain what it is|magazine=w:CNN|url=https://www.cnn.com/2024/08/21/science/hypervelocity-star-escape-milky-way|date=2024-08-21|passage=By combining the data from multiple telescopes, astronomers determined the star’s position and '''velocity''' in space, allowing them to predict that it will exit the Milky Way at some point.}}
# {{U|rapidity}} of motion.
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:speed}}
#: {{ux|en|The train was travelling at a slower '''velocity''' than usual.}}
#* {{RQ:Pynchon Mason & Dixon|39|395|passage=Over the winter-solid Roads, goes a great seething,— of mounted younger Gentlemen riding together by the dozens upon rented horses, Express Messengers in love with pure '''Velocity''', Disgruntl'd Suitors with Pistols stuff'd in their Spatterdashes, seal'd Waggons not even a western Black-Boy would think of detaining.}}
# The rate of occurrence.
# {{lb|en|economics}} The number of times that an average unit of [[currency]] is spent during a specific period of time.

